hstr
------------------------------------------
Are you looking for a command that you used recently? Do you want to avoid the
need to write long commands over and over again despite you used them recently?
Are you looking for a tool that is able to manage your favorite commands?

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libncursesw10-6.5+20240427-1
  libreadline8-8.3-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libncurses-devel-6.5+20240427-1
  libreadline-devel-8.3-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/dvorka/hstr

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/dvorka/hstr/archive/refs/tags/v.3.3.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack hstr-3.3-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./hstr-3.3-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/hstr-3.3-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/hstr-3.3-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(hstr)
  /usr/bin/hh.exe
  /usr/bin/hstr.exe
  /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/hstr
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/hstr.README
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/CONFIGURATION.md
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/Changelog
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/DEVELOPER-DOCUMENTATION.md
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/README.md
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/SECURITY.md
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/USER-DOCUMENTATION.md
  /usr/share/doc/hstr/hstr-v2.gif
  /usr/share/man/man1/hstr.1.gz

